# .gitignore — publishing/src/
#
# Template-owned; copier update keeps it current. Project-wide rules belong in the root .gitignore.
# No inline comments in this file: Git reads a # after a pattern as part of the pattern.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered deliverables, burned versions and thumbnail PNGs
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Made by the toolkit from the master, the captions and the thumbnail layouts on request:
# regenerable, and too large for plain Git. Each piece's renders sit in a folder named for it
# (renders/<piece>/), and only what no piece owns (a feed's upload copy, a show's cover
# encodes) at the folder's top; the pattern below ignores every folder inside renders/ whole,
# so a per-piece folder needs no pattern of its own. The folder's README stays tracked, so the
# folder and its explanation exist in every checkout. Never force a render past this rule.
/renders/*
!/renders/README.md
